LIMITATIONS
===========================================================================
- other players MUST be using some addon that has LibSpec embedded. The
  usual one is big/littlewigs (I guess). Could also say that everyone needs
  to run PetesDefensiveHistory.. :)

- abilities with both dynamic cooldown reduction and charges are hard to handle reasonably
  the problem: CDR and charges must be handled in the opposite way
        * abilities with charges: cooldown swipes are handled differently:
          when the ability is used before its cooldown is up, the cooldown swipe is left
          alone to continue its current recharge. this is how charge abilities are supposed
          to work, where one charge recovers at a time.
        * abilities with dynamic CDR: since the cooldown reduction events can't be tracked,
          the best we can do is put an incorrect timer+swipe for the maximum possible CD.
          it is wrong, but it is still better than no information. since it is wrong,
          the ability could be used before its cooldown swipe finishes. when that happens,
          the correct behavior is to cancel the previous swipe and start a new one.
    - the current behavior is to ignore CDR entirely. when used with full charges, the
      cooldown swipe begins and it propagates itself at the full CD timer. it is assumed
      that the next recharge doesn't start until the first recharge is completely full
        * can do better than this. each time the ability is observed is extra information
          that can help bring the timer closer to the truth.
        * currently the events are entirely ignored. the code just ensures that the
          numQueued counter never passes the max number of charges
    - even after improving, it still might be a good idea to add an option to disable
      inference for CDR+charge abilities, sending them to the tray instead. maybe one
      checkbox that affects all such abilities (and dynamically determines if the needed
      talents are chosen).
    - abilities:
        ----- Rotational CDR (definitely not trackable)
        * disc priest: pain suppression
            - CDR on PW:S casts
        * prot pal: GoAK
            - CDR on holy power spenders
        * prot war: shield wall
            - CDR on rage use and shield slams
        ----- CDR on large cooldowns (e.g., resets) or other weird circumstances
        * balance druid: incarn/celestial alignment
            - weird keeper of the grove talent that reduces cooldown based on time spent
              with ability off CD. maybe modelable?
        * aug evoker: scales
            - potentially trackable since the CDR is attached to a long
              cooldown that may itself be trackable
        * frost mage: ice cold/ice block
            - not really. this a case where cold snap (ability reset) is treated as CDR
              because it seemed convenient at the time



