- handle instant inference in the cases where it's possible
    * for buffs that are unique without duration info
    * align these buffs next to frames omniCD style
    * these never enter the history tray
- add instant tracking
- better inference using cooldown tracking
    - e.g.: prot paladin has AD=8s and GoAK=8s so they can't be distinguished.
      if AD and GoAK are used in sequence, we don't know which was used first, but
      the only way to have 2 8s buffs is if they were both used. so now can infer
      AD is on cd and one charge of GoAK is used. so if we see another 8s buff on
      the paladin, we know it was charge 2 of GoAK and now both charges are on CD
      for some time. AD will probably come off CD during this period, meaning that
      the next CD is likely AD.
        - gets a little murkier since GoAK is also a CDR spell
- separate the bookkeeping of updatePdhGroupSolution() from the inference logic
